{"title":"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Best_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Best Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">Triangle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb0f1d8a43539dbc3355734bafb2bfd855b5f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Length\" title=\"Length\">length</a> 43, 13, and 48, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumscribe\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Circumscribe\">circumscribed</a> around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intersection\" title=\"Intersection\">intersection</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular_bisector\" title=\"Perpendicular bisector\">perpendicular bisector</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> that is not on the same side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f1dcbb9badfd3447d4e7351678b7d71ea9bff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integers</a> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility\" title=\"Divisibility\"> divisible</a> by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a> of any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a>. Find the greatest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/2/1d26a03d410fa1cc4f3af6e22ef47a7452804e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + \\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Best_Solution\">Best Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Best Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We set up a trivial coordinate bash. Let A = (0,0), C = (48,0), B = (83/2, 13√3/2). We find the coordinates of the circumcenter to be 24, -11√3/3. The radius is 43√3.Then the coordinate of point D are 24, -18√3. The answer is then 6 + √43, which yields 12.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The perpendicular bisector of any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chord\" title=\"Chord\">chord</a> of any circle passes through the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Center\" title=\"Center\">center</a> of that circle.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Midpoint\" title=\"Midpoint\">midpoint</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the length of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_of_a_Point_Theorem\" title=\"Power of a Point Theorem\">Power of a Point Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/2/752673b567257bc742b6465cba5e57ef5978d589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD \\cdot (2R - MD) = AM \\cdot MC = 24^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"295\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa606fcdbf84a39d12df0fcf5c3779c45144e00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = MD^2 -2R\\cdot MD 24^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"193\" height=\"15\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2ed3d2205ea679b9dd0904e0b799c591e50361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD^2 = MD^2 + AM^2 = MD^2 + 24^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"279\" height=\"16\" />.  \n</p><p>Let's compute the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumradius\" title=\"Circumradius\">circumradius</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />: By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/931d76c7a764b2ceb6a2997c60fd333f662a6f86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos B = \\frac{AB^2 + BC^2 - CA^2}{2\\cdot AB\\cdot BC} = \\frac{43^2 + 13^2 - 48^2}{2\\cdot43\\cdot13} = -\\frac{11}{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"431\" height=\"39\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a0e9eaf17d856946b09e7f03354519045afbef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2R = \\frac{AC}{\\sin B} = \\frac{48}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(-\\frac{11}{43}\\right)^2}} = \\frac{86}{\\sqrt 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -31px\" width=\"274\" height=\"56\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84634cd3b2d1d3e71cd4e2e0c7825635bec63e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\frac{43}{\\sqrt 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"65\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Now we can use this to compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f00f55b6b1cf59b8a3b3687a2b9aed8b37578c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.  By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_formula\" title=\"Quadratic formula\">quadratic formula</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e038f7d38684748b5c12fbe6ff111bbb3d5223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MD = \\frac{2R + \\sqrt{4R^2 - 4\\cdot24^2}}{2} = \\frac{43}{\\sqrt 3} + \\frac{11}{\\sqrt3} = 18\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"394\" height=\"45\" />.  (We only take the positive sign because <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angle</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Obtuse_angle\" title=\"Obtuse angle\"> obtuse</a> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b31782c8439bb79194a830084c6c61a1feb22bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{MD}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"15\" /> is the longer of the two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line_segment\" title=\"Line segment\"> segments</a> into which the chord <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> divides the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Diameter\" title=\"Diameter\">diameter</a>.)  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/c/b2c816203b6731d33238fde56d67678f4b4efe61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD^2 = MD^2 + 24^2 = 1548$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e55472bb594e5d58f8012748192a1380cb99c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 6\\sqrt{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21ebdc79fa99d857f49ec400dc7af8e67f639ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 &lt; 6 + \\sqrt{43} &lt; 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/3/f332a8b8cd4172b41969a199989acc5a933d042f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$012$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cd5c7783a52516b2f417e6c2565042f9fa9c7b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC = b$\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85c28a58e394ee9fc1102c60e5aaacc3a333995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = DC = x$\" width=\"117\" height=\"13\" />. Since ABCD is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cyclic_quadrilateral\" title=\"Cyclic quadrilateral\">cyclic quadrilateral</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3ca6c53270fa8b3f64d477689e49a92f54a0bae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> degrees. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9c3fa398600f960fd25a6ff7e8d678cbd6f323.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48^2 = 43^2 + 13^2 - (2)(43)(13)\\cos a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"273\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cb5e98ca78942e930e7ebe090d75e67fce69789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos a = -\\frac{11}{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cb5e98ca78942e930e7ebe090d75e67fce69789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos a = -\\frac{11}{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7eaf5f292779cb9d1e24df63a1e5b0a02cf1d804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos b$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c7579c0f37b1879d2517b10bac838c40b8dc3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{11}{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. Using the Law of Cosines on triangle ADC, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51ffca5c8980330d09d77eda62b17d74a9133fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48^2 = 2x^2 - 2x^2 \\cos b = 2x^2(1 - \\cos b) = 2x^2(\\frac{32}{43})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"382\" height=\"38\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2a01a4a537d8c8ae283179d50034a7ae36907c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 6 + {\\sqrt 43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> which is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16dcde358a301b519e85db633abdf0fe89f0f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Extend the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/4/944ba602cbe46ab39832591c92962190a4c70854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACE = \\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/8/1089b2128be64442dd3f1743cbb88c5a681be222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACBE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic. Further, note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a24f79f0c3ca735f4177c04eb8c341bea435b29a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC = \\angle AEC = \\angle AED + \\angle DEC = \\angle ACD + \\angle DAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"456\" height=\"16\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f46b0985084bb1f09200fb0b6499f8079577e6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADCE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic.\n</p><p>Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/3/df3dc0ace8eb4dd2dd5f37038a159dbe365c044a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/7/067cd4b5b8b4006cf65056c36f17a51fa1f8da9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACD = \\angle DAC = \\frac{\\angle ABC}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"222\" height=\"39\" />. The problem then boils down to finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf9f2cb60225dbaf3a0d2d56264ef5fec16b3e22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\frac{B}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"74\" height=\"45\" />, which we know we can do.\n</p><p>By Heron's formula and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/2/e5247650c5040309690323b27391e1a96792eed8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs = A$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, we yield that the inradius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f7e99b6a177dd82046ee2ae91b50c143a72b417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the incenter and the foot of the perpendicular from the incenter to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5a7a5dcf4aa1bf79a0e02edfdb0e98519e261b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BP = s - b = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/3/3d38ce166c48523bf239ee0f96bc67a0a66de2c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI = \\sqrt{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"21\" /> by the Pythagorean theorem. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e03e69744c05e4bfef650db0c4ed898a50160d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\frac{B}{2}\\right) = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{43}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"136\" height=\"45\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e55472bb594e5d58f8012748192a1380cb99c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 6\\sqrt{43}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />, by examining right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/0/bc0efa6d115704d4a8ba9138ab4da8eaa9dc6671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AMD$\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/e/21ebdc79fa99d857f49ec400dc7af8e67f639ac6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 &lt; 6 + \\sqrt{43} &lt; 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/6/f16dcde358a301b519e85db633abdf0fe89f0f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{012}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems/Problem 14\"> Previous Problem</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_4_2006-2007_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems\">Mock AIME 4 2006-2007 Problems</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017044746\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 389/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14652/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4425:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017044746 and revision id 285245. Rendering was triggered because: p